 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios Instacart shares hit an all-time high on Monday, before a slight Tuesday pullback, following reports that the grocery delivery company is nearing a sale to DoorDash. 

 Both WSJ and Reuters put around a $17 billion price on the prospective deal, which would work out to over $70 per Instacart share, although neither said if DoorDash would pay all cash or cash and stock. 
 
